# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=..., set by the tsan test preset). Every entry needs a
# justification. Prefer fixing the code; TSan runs nightly and is advisory (docs/testing.md).
#
# libarrow and libparquet (conda-forge) are not built with TSan: the synchronization inside Arrow's thread pools and
# futures (e.g. the I/O pool that pre-buffers Parquet column chunks) is invisible to TSan, so a buffer that an Arrow
# I/O thread frees after the reader is done is reported as racing with the reader's earlier memcpy (first seen in the
# nightly of 2026-09-26: BaseMemoryPoolImpl<SystemAllocator>::Free vs snappy decompression). Suppress race reports
# whose stacks run through these libraries. Deliberately `race:` and not `called_from_lib:`: ignoring the libraries'
# interceptors hides their mutex locks, and an unlock that Arrow's inlined future callbacks then perform in another
# library is reported as "unlock of an unlocked mutex". Races confined to our own code are still reported.
race:libarrow.so
race:libparquet.so

# DuckDB 2.0.0 (conda-forge, test oracle). Recheck these Linux reports with pixi run tsan on
# the next DuckDB upgrade. Access stacks: https://github.com/ydb-campus/antb1/issues/271
# Nightly runs 45616991058 and 45819101495 cover the signatures below.
#
# Parquet scans: a worker releases its read-ahead task as the consumer frees the job. Other
# reports pair the worker's file read with a Thrift buffer read, or buffer allocation with
# destruction of the consumer's ReadHead vector. Reproduced by oracle and differential tests.
race:duckdb::ReadAheadIOTask::~ReadAheadIOTask(
race:duckdb::ThriftFileTransport::read(
race:std::vector<duckdb::shared_ptr<duckdb::ReadHead,*>::_M_erase_at_end(

# Parquet fixture creation: row-group preparation races with writer initialization, and copies
# of column names race with allocation of the integer or struct column writer. The dictionary
# predicate integration test also reports a worker copying identifiers as DuckDB reads them.
race:duckdb::ParquetWriter::PrepareRowGroup(
race:duckdb::make_uniq<duckdb::StandardColumnWriter<long, long, duckdb::ParquetCastOperator>,
race:duckdb::make_uniq<duckdb::StructColumnWriter,
race:duckdb::IdentifiersToStrings[abi:cxx11](

# Differential tests also report DuckDB's bundled jemalloc initializing a decay mutex while
# another thread acquires it. Match the initializer specific to DuckDB's copy of jemalloc.
race:^duckdb_je_decay_init$
